        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module checks whether each extracted data column is documented in a codebook or README, and flags documented variables that never appear in the data.",
          "We examined 1 codebook/README/label source and 4 data columns across 1 file.",
          "#### Column Documentation",
          "::: {.panel-tabset}\n\n## s.csv\n\n\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Column = c(\"grp\", \"mood\", \"sleep_hours\", \"id\"), \n    Documented = c(\"conflict\", \"conflict\", \"conflict\", \"no\"), \n    Label = c(\"Experimental condition\", \"Positive affect rated from 1 to 5\", \n    \"Hours slept the previous night\", NA), \"Codebook Variable\" = c(\"grp\", \n    \"mood\", \"sleep_hours\", NA), Source = c(\"README.md\", \"README.md\", \n    \"README.md\", NA), Status = c(\"ambiguous_experiment\", \"ambiguous_experiment\", \n    \"ambiguous_experiment\", \"unlabelled\")), row.names = c(NA, \n4L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 25, FALSE)\n```\n\n\n:::",
          "#### Conflicting or Ambiguous Definitions\n\n3 matched columns have more than one codebook definition, or a definition scoped to a different experiment. These are matched to a codebook but need manual resolution before the label can be trusted.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = c(\"s.csv\", \"s.csv\", \"s.csv\"), Column = c(\"mood\", \n\"sleep_hours\", \"grp\"), \"Conflicting Labels\" = c(\"Positive affect rated from 1 to 5\", \n\"Hours slept the previous night\", \"Experimental condition\"), \n    Sources = c(\"README.md\", \"README.md\", \"README.md\"), Issue = c(\"ambiguous_experiment\", \n    \"ambiguous_experiment\", \"ambiguous_experiment\")), row.names = 2:4, class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "LLM model 'mock/cbc' reviewed ambiguous cases (parsed 1 file, matched 0 columns, merged 0 labels)."
        ]
